recommendedPlan.change:
Add `@Composable fun GlassPillButton(onClick: () -> Unit, modifier: Modifier = Modifier, enabled: Boolean = true, prominent: Boolean = true, enterProgress: () -> Float = { 1f }, content: @Composable RowScope.() -> Unit)`.

Build it on GlassPanel, NOT LiquidButton. LiquidButton rebuilds its drawBackdrop chain on every recomposition (LiquidButton.kt:84-135), and these pills sit on screens that recompose per keystroke or per selection. GlassPanel arguments:
- `shape = com.kyant.shapes.Capsule()`, `heavy = false`, `refractionHeight = 24.dp`, `refractionAmount = 48.dp` (a light panel halves these to LiquidButton's 12/24);
- `pressScale = LiquidMotion.ButtonPressScale`;
- `tint = glassPillTint(palette, prominent, enabled)` and `accent = if (prominent && enabled) palette.accent else Color.Unspecified`;
- `onClick = if (enabled) onClick else null`, `interactive = enabled`;
- `enterProgress`.

Content is a `Row(Modifier.heightIn(min = 48.dp).padding(horizontal = 20.dp), spacedBy(8.dp), CenterVertically)`, with content alpha 0.38 when disabled (graphicsLayer).

Semantics: GlassPanel adds Role.Button only when it has an onClick (GlassPanel.kt:193-203), so add `Modifier.semantics(mergeDescendants = true) { role = Role.Button; if (!enabled) disabled() }` here.

Add the pure helper `internal fun glassPillTint(palette: GlassPalette, prominent: Boolean, enabled: Boolean): Color`: accent.copy(alpha = 0.38f) when prominent and enabled (the 'lit' value GlassHeaderActionOrb uses, ScreenChrome.kt:101-108), otherwise palette.tintSubtle.

KDoc should state the kit rules: it reads LocalGlassBackdrop and is never a layerBackdrop reader's ancestor.

Write the dated handoff note required by AGENTS.md:
- what changed per file, in both modes;
- the Android-specific divergences from iOS:
  - the glass refracts the ambient, not the player;
  - Material uses the M3 FAB-menu morph;
  - Stats and the three sheets were already compliant;
- what was compiled and tested, and what wasn't;
- a checkbox list for Hoa's Pixel 10 Pro: queue open, drag, fling and predictive back; tap above the sheet dismisses and never hits the player; menu morph open and close plus each action; undo bar; toolbar toggles and their selected state with TalkBack; the four glass pills including Quick Fill disabled; full-player chips; light and dark; 'Disable blur all over' and Material mode; frame times during queue open and the morph (`adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo com.theveloper.pixelplay.debug framestats`, ONLY after asking before driving the phone).
Commit messages are plain-English imperatives with the attribution lines.

tests:
